    ],
    "design": [
      "/Users/maparent/OpenSource/discourse-graph/openspec/changes/cross-app-asset-references/design.md"
    ],
    "tasks": [
      "/Users/maparent/OpenSource/discourse-graph/openspec/changes/cross-app-asset-references/tasks.md"
    ]
  },
  "progress": {
    "total": 20,
    "complete": 0,
    "remaining": 20
  },
  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "1",
      "description": "1.1 Add a nullable `filename` column to `FileReference`, add it to the `my_file_references` select list, and regenerate `dbTypes.ts`; verify a row written with a name is visible through the view as a non-privileged user, that existing callers still compile, and that the garbage-collection triggers, `file_access` and the bucket policy are untouched",
      "done": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "description": "1.2 Add a `filename` parameter to `addFile`, threaded into both the insert and the duplicate-key update; verify a re-publish under a changed name updates the stored name rather than keeping the old one",
      "done": false
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "description": "1.3 Define the shared asset reference type and add fixtures for a stored asset and an unresolvable one; verify the fixtures typecheck and are consumable from both apps",
      "done": false
    },
    {
      "id": "4",
      "description": "1.4 Choose the size limit for each transfer direction and record it in the design with its rationale; verify each is a named constant covered by a test asserting that an asset above it is skipped and reported rather than throwing",
      "done": false
    },
    {
      "id": "5",
      "description": "2.1 Find asset references in a node's `full` markdown; verify unit tests cover an image embed, a non-image embed, a bare URL and an external link",
      "done": false
    },
    {
      "id": "6",
      "description": "2.2 Fetch one referenced asset from Roam storage and resolve its original name from the object descriptor; verify unit tests cover a descriptor with the name key present and one with it absent, falling back to the storage uid",
      "done": false
    },
    {
      "id": "7",
      "description": "2.3 Copy a fetched asset through `addFile` with its `filename`, skipping anything above the cap; verify copying identical content twice stores one copy, and that an over-cap asset returns a skip result",
      "done": false
    },
    {
      "id": "8",
      "description": "2.4 Add the asset stage to publish, running after content upsert; verify a node with an image publishes with a reference recorded whose `filepath` is the URL from the markdown, and that the published markdown is unchanged by the stage",
      "done": false
    },
    {
      "id": "9",
      "description": "2.5 Report per-asset failures in the publish result; verify a node whose asset cannot be fetched still publishes with its content intact and the failure in the result",
      "done": false
    },
    {
      "id": "10",
      "description": "3.1 Use `filename` for the local name when present, otherwise decompose `filepath`; verify a reference recorded with a name imports under a readable local name with no part of its token in the path",
      "done": false
    },
    {
      "id": "11",
      "description": "3.2 Disambiguate a colliding target path, keyed on content hash; verify two distinct assets recorded under the same name both import intact, and that re-importing an unchanged node neither renames nor duplicates",
      "done": false
    },
    {
      "id": "12",
      "description": "3.3 Verify by regression test that a reference with a null `filename` imports exactly as it did before this change",
      "done": false
    },
    {
      "id": "13",
      "description": "4.1 Add the graph-level asset registry accessor; verify a write followed by a read returns the same map, and that the page and block are created when absent",
      "done": false
    },
    {
      "id": "14",
      "description": "4.2 Copy one asset from shared storage into Roam storage, recording hash to URL after the upload returns; verify the same hash twice performs one upload, that all five upload return shapes unwrap to a URL, and that an over-cap asset returns a skip",
      "done": false
    },
    {
      "id": "15",
      "description": "5.1 Resolve each reference through its recorded row, leaving a token unchanged only when no row matches; verify an image, a non-media asset and an external link each produce the right result, with the external link untouched",
      "done": false
    },
    {
      "id": "16",
      "description": "5.2 Label a non-media link with its recorded name; verify the rendered link text shows the name rather than a storage URL",
      "done": false
    },
    {
      "id": "17",
      "description": "5.3 Add the asset stage to materialization between fetch-content and replace-page-content; verify in a real Roam graph that an imported node's image renders, and that re-syncing it uploads nothing",
      "done": false
    },
    {
      "id": "18",
      "description": "5.4 Verify a node published from Roam and imported into a second Roam graph resolves through its recorded row and stores that graph's own copy, rather than passing the origin URL through",
      "done": false
    },
    {
      "id": "19",
      "description": "6.1 Verify the degradation path across both directions: an asset that fails at publication leaves its token in the published markdown, imports without breaking the node body, and is reported at both ends",
      "done": false
    },
    {
      "id": "20",
      "description": "6.2 Run `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` then `pnpm ci:validate` from the repository root and resolve any failures",
      "done": false
    }
  ],
  "state": "ready",
  "instruction": "Read context files, work through pending tasks, mark complete as you go.\nPause if you hit blockers or need clarification.",
  "root": {
    "path": "/Users/maparent/OpenSource/discourse-graph",
    "source": "nearest"
  }
}

